Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:05:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mcp): add HITL approval gate to push_file/merge_pr, wire
 guard tests into CI

Retracts the gap left by #757: that PR added a repo allowlist, a
protected-branch guard and correct destructiveHint values, but the write
path still had no human approval step.

1. HITL gate (the main gap)
   github.push_file and github.merge_pr now call requestWriteApproval()
   before doing anything. Roles below admin (agent/rank 1) get an
   approval request, the call returns HITL_APPROVAL_REQUIRED with the
   request ID and writes NOTHING. The caller retries with the approved
   approvalRequestId. admin+ is exempt (they are the approvers), matching
   the guardian.tools.ts:331 merge_pr pattern instead of inventing a
   second convention.

   assertApproved() is fail-closed: missing ID, unknown ID, PENDING and
   REJECTED all deny.

2. test:github-guards wired into CI
   The test file shipped with #757 but no workflow ran it, so a broken
   guard would still have shown green. Now runs in
   syntax-and-governance-gate.

3. AGENTS.md corrected
   It claimed bot-authored PRs skip automation via
   github.actor != 'github-actions[bot]'. That condition was removed in
   62a3dee. Replaced with the actual invariant: the loop closes because
   the patch file is deleted after merge, and the residual force-push risk
   is stated.

Verified locally, not assumed:
- tsc --noEmit: 0 errors
- npm run test:github-guards: all pass (incl. 8 new HITL assertions)
- workflow YAML parses; 24 jobs; test wired in syntax-and-governance-gate

Test run caught two real bugs during development: the helper is async
(fixed), and HITL link signing needs MCP_ADMIN_KEY (test now sets it).
